{
  "format": "resend-lab",
  "version": 1,
  "kind": "guided",
  "topic": "Observing",
  "title": "Watch ARP and ping",
  "brief": "Two PCs on a switch, ready to go. Ping PC-B from PC-A and watch what happens, frame by frame: then answer from what you saw.",
  "network": {
    "devices": [
      {
        "id": 1,
        "kind": "host",
        "name": "PC-A",
        "x": 80,
        "y": 90,
        "ports": [
          {
            "ipv4": "192.168.1.10/24"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": 2,
        "kind": "host",
        "name": "PC-B",
        "x": 580,
        "y": 90,
        "ports": [
          {
            "ipv4": "192.168.1.20/24"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": 3,
        "kind": "switch",
        "name": "Switch",
        "x": 330,
        "y": 300
      }
    ],
    "links": [
      {
        "id": 1,
        "a": {
          "device": 1,
          "port": 1
        },
        "b": {
          "device": 3,
          "port": 1
        }
      },
      {
        "id": 2,
        "a": {
          "device": 2,
          "port": 1
        },
        "b": {
          "device": 3,
          "port": 2
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "locks": [
    {
      "device": "PC-A"
    },
    {
      "device": "PC-B"
    },
    {
      "device": "Switch"
    }
  ],
  "goals": [
    {
      "id": "asked",
      "kind": "observed",
      "text": "PC-A asks with ARP who has 192.168.1.20",
      "device": "PC-A",
      "record": "arp-request",
      "for": "192.168.1.20"
    },
    {
      "id": "answered",
      "kind": "observed",
      "text": "PC-B answers the ARP request",
      "device": "PC-B",
      "record": "arp-reply"
    },
    {
      "id": "learned",
      "kind": "observed",
      "text": "The switch learns where the PCs are",
      "device": "Switch",
      "record": "mac-learned"
    },
    {
      "id": "replied",
      "kind": "observed",
      "text": "PC-A's ping gets its Echo Reply",
      "device": "PC-A",
      "record": "echo-reply"
    },
    {
      "id": "mac",
      "kind": "answer",
      "text": "Which destination MAC does PC-A's Echo Request carry?",
      "from": "PC-A",
      "to": "192.168.1.20",
      "quantity": "first-hop-mac"
    },
    {
      "id": "ttl",
      "kind": "answer",
      "text": "What is the TTL of the Echo Reply when it reaches PC-A?",
      "from": "PC-A",
      "to": "192.168.1.20",
      "quantity": "reply-ttl"
    }
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Select PC-A, write 192.168.1.20 in the action bar, press Send, then Run.",
    "Step through the run: the first frame is an ARP request, sent to every port, the broadcast address ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff.",
    "Select an event on the timeline and open its Frame tab: the Echo Request's Ethernet header names the MAC it goes to.",
    "Open the Echo Reply that comes back in the Frame tab and read its TTL, then write both answers and press Check."
  ],
  "hints": [
    "PC-A needs PC-B's MAC before it can send the Echo Request: that is what ARP is for.",
    "The switch's MAC table, in its inspector, fills as frames arrive.",
    "A TTL goes down by one at each router. Here there is none."
  ],
  "solution": {
    "network": {
      "devices": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "kind": "host",
          "name": "PC-A",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 90,
          "ports": [
            {
              "ipv4": "192.168.1.10/24"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "kind": "host",
          "name": "PC-B",
          "x": 580,
          "y": 90,
          "ports": [
            {
              "ipv4": "192.168.1.20/24"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "kind": "switch",
          "name": "Switch",
          "x": 330,
          "y": 300
        }
      ],
      "links": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "a": {
            "device": 1,
            "port": 1
          },
          "b": {
            "device": 3,
            "port": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "a": {
            "device": 2,
            "port": 1
          },
          "b": {
            "device": 3,
            "port": 2
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "commands": [
      {
        "from": "PC-A",
        "ping": "192.168.1.20"
      }
    ],
    "answers": {
      "mac": "02:00:00:00:00:02",
      "ttl": "64"
    }
  }
